[38;2;124;124;124mWe need to find all real numbers $c$ such that $i(p) \leq c \cdot d(p)$ holds [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mfor all positive integers $n$ and all permutations $p$ of $\{1, 2, \ldots, n\}$.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mHere:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- $d(p) = \sum_{k=1}^n |p(k) - k|$ is the total displacement[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- $i(p)$ is the number of inversions (pairs $(i,j)$ with $i < j$ and $p(i) > [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mp(j)$)[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWe need to find the infimum of $i(p)/d(p)$ over all permutations (with $d(p) > [0m
