[38;2;124;124;124m$d(p) - d(p') = |p(k) - k| + |p(k+1) - (k+1)| - |p(k+1) - k| - |p(k) - (k+1)|$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet $a = p(k)$, $b = p(k+1)$, with $a > b$ (adjacent inversion).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m$d(p) - d(p') = |a - k| + |b - (k+1)| - |b - k| - |a - (k+1)|$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me compute this for various cases.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mCase 1: $a > k$ and $b < k+1$ (i.e., $a \geq k+1$ and $b \leq k$).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$d(p) - d(p') = (a - k) + (k+1 - b) - |b-k| - |a-k-1|$.[0m
