[38;2;124;124;124mSince $a \geq k+1$: $|a-k-1| = a - k - 1$.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$= (a-k) + (k+1-b) - (k-b) - (a-k-1) = a - k + k + 1 - b - k + b - a + k + 1 = [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m2$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo $d(p) - d(p') = 2$, meaning $d(p') = d(p) - 2$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mCase 2: $a > k+1$ and $b > k$ (i.e., $a \geq k+2$ and $b \geq k+1$, but $b < a$ [0m[38;2;124;124;124mso $b \leq a-1$; also $b \geq k+1$).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$d(p) - d(p') = (a-k) + (b-k-1) - (b-k) - (a-k-1) = a-k+b-k-1-b+k-a+k+1 = 0$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo $d(p') = d(p)$. The displacement doesn't change![0m

[38;2;124;124;124mCase 3: $a \leq k$ and $b < k+1$ (i.e., $a \leq k$ and $b \leq k$).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$d(p) - d(p') = (k-a) + (k+1-b) - |b-k| - |a-k-1|$.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$b \leq k$: $|b-k| = k-b$.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$a \leq k$: $|a-k-1| = k+1-a$.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$= (k-a) + (k+1-b) - (k-b) - (k+1-a) = k-a+k+1-b-k+b-k-1+a = 0$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mAgain $d(p') = d(p)$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mCase 4: $a \leq k$ and $b \geq k+1$. But $a > b$ and $a \leq k < k+1 \leq b$, so[0m[38;2;124;124;124m$a < b$, contradiction. So this case is impossible.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo in Case 1, $d$ decreases by 2 and $i$ decreases by 1, so $i/d$ changes in a [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcomplex way. In Cases 2 and 3, $d$ stays the same and $i$ decreases by 1.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThis means: starting from $p$ and doing bubble sort to reach identity, each step[0m[38;2;124;124;124meither keeps $d$ the same or decreases it by 2. And each step decreases $i$ by [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m1.[0m

